Priced To Sell — A Rare Opportunity In A Highly Sought-After Macleod Setting
11 HILLTOP AVENUE, MACLEOD
IMPORTANT PURCHASER NOTICE:
The property has major structural defects resulting from previous termite damage. While no active termites have currently been identified, structural damage remains. Purchasers are strongly advised to undertake their own independent building, pest and structural inspections with suitably qualified professionals prior to making any decision to purchase and should satisfy themselves as to the condition of the property, the extent of the damage and the likely costs associated with any required rectification works.

Now priced to sell, with the asking price taking into account the works required, this substantial residence presents an outstanding opportunity for buyers seeking a generous allotment in a highly sought-after Macleod location and who are prepared to undertake the necessary improvements.

A home where today's comfort meets tomorrow's possibilities, this warm and welcoming residence offers the space every family desires and the potential every buyer hopes to find. Enjoying a prized position in one of Macleod's most desirable pockets, its adaptable floorplan, multiple living spaces and generous 767m² allotment (approx.) provide an excellent foundation for those seeking a property with scope to renovate, improve and add value over time.

The surprisingly spacious interior provides an adaptable layout with multiple living zones and plenty of scope for those looking to create their ideal home. Four bedrooms are serviced by a family bathroom featuring dual basins, while a separate lounge and dining room is anchored by a gas log fire and complemented by an expansive open-plan living and meals area.

Large, light-filled spaces, timber floors and a gorgeous garden outlook create a welcoming atmosphere, with the living area extending from the kitchen to an entertainer's deck. Covered for year-round use, the deck overlooks a striking garden offering established greenery and paved alfresco pockets, creating a private setting for outdoor enjoyment.
Decorative cornices, a laundry with a convenient second toilet, robes to each bedroom, ducted heating, a garden shed, and a gated carport supplementing a single garage with shelving and a workbench complete the property's extensive list of features.

Tucked away in a well-connected address that offers everything a family needs, parklands, sporting facilities and quality schools are all close by, as are Macleod and Watsonia Villages with their train stations, cafés, eateries, supermarkets and entertainment options.

Purchasers should conduct their own comprehensive due diligence and obtain independent professional advice regarding the property's structural condition, previous termite damage, required rectification works and associated costs before entering into a contract.


